[center]
[size=3]Find your best fights and your best gear, simulated with the game's own combat.[/size]
[size=2][color=#8e96a4]Version {{version}} · checked with Melvor Idle 2 {{game_version}}[/color][/size]
[/center]
[line]
CS2 runs each fight many times in a hidden copy of the game, with your gear, levels, prayers, potions, pets and bonuses as they are, so its numbers follow the game as it would play.

[b][color=#3cc4c0]Results[/color][/b]: every target ranked by XP, kills and more, with deaths per hour.
{{media:screenshots/modio/01-results.png}}
[b][color=#3cc4c0]Compare[/color][/b]: two setups on the same fights, side by side.
{{media:screenshots/modio/02-compare.png}}
[b][color=#3cc4c0]Setup[/color][/b]: try any gear, levels, prayers, potions, pets and more, owned or not.
{{media:screenshots/modio/03-setup.png}}
[b][color=#3cc4c0]Best setup[/color][/b]: the best gear for a target, a cheaper option, and the upgrades worth chasing.
{{media:screenshots/modio/05-search-and-upgrades.png}}
[b][color=#3cc4c0]Rare drops[/color][/b]: the chance per kill, and roughly when the first one should drop.
{{media:screenshots/modio/07-rare-drops.png}}
[b][color=#3cc4c0]Slayer masters[/color][/b]: the best loadout for each master, and which tasks to block.
{{media:screenshots/modio/08-blocks.png}}

Open it with [b]Sim[/b] in the game's header. A guide and a short tour are in its About.

[line]
[size=5][b][color=#3cc4c0]Install[/color][/b][/size]
For the Windows version of the game.
[list=1]
[*]Close Melvor Idle 2.
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab and extract everything into the game's folder, next to [font=Courier New]Melvor2.exe[/font] (in Steam: right-click the game, Manage, Browse local files). Replace files if asked.
[*]Start the game and open the simulator with [b]Sim[/b] in the game's header.
[/list]

[b]Update[/b]
Close the game and extract the new zip over the old files. Your settings and saved runs stay.
[color=#e0b84a][b]Preview[/b]: CS2 stays in preview until Melvor Idle 2 has official mod support. It's a large and complex mod that will get updates throughout Early Access.[/color]

[b]Uninstall[/b]
Close the game and delete [font=Courier New]mods/CombatSimulator2/[/font] in the game's folder; its settings and saved runs go with it. If no other mod is installed this way, also delete [font=Courier New]winmm.dll[/font] and the [font=Courier New]mods/[/font] folder.

[b]What it installs[/b]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]winmm.dll[/font] next to [font=Courier New]Melvor2.exe[/font], which starts the mod.
[*][font=Courier New]mods/CombatSimulator2/[/font]: the mod, its loader ([font=Courier New]loader/[/font]), and its settings, saved runs, logs and bug reports.
[/list]

[b]Other mods[/b]
CS2 needs no other mod. It works alongside Melvor Mod Loader and the mods that use it.

[b]Your game[/b]
Fights run in a hidden second copy of the game that closes with it. CS2 never changes your game or saves, and sends nothing online.

[line]
[size=5][b][color=#3cc4c0]Bugs and feedback[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Save bug report[/b] in CS2's About writes a zip with CS2's logs and settings, your recent runs and your character's save (leave the save out in Settings). Attach it to your report:
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/Crashv0/CombatSimulator2/issues/new?template=bug-report.yml]Report a bug[/url] on GitHub, or in the Bugs tab here
[*][url=https://discord.com/channels/625838709203271680/1029950790254731334]#mod-bug-reports[/url] on the Melvor Idle Discord
[/list]
[b]Feedback[/b]: ideas, or issues that aren't bugs, [url=https://github.com/Crashv0/CombatSimulator2/issues/new?template=feedback.yml]on GitHub[/url].
[b]Translations[/b]: help on [url=https://crowdin.com/project/combat-simulator-2]Crowdin[/url], or [url=https://github.com/Crashv0/CombatSimulator2/issues/new?template=translation.yml]request a language or report a mistake[/url].
[b]Source and changelog[/b]: [url=https://github.com/Crashv0/CombatSimulator2]GitHub[/url].
[line]
